# `catalog seed --fixture <path>` writes real application records. Through 0.1.0
# one such file was committed as `fixtures/apps.seed.jsonl` AND listed in `files`,
# so 86 real app records shipped to the public npm registry. Seed output is
# generated data: produce it on demand, keep it outside the repo. The one
# synthetic fixture below is the deliberate exception.
*.seed.jsonl
!fixtures/apps.seed.jsonl
